### Register a new user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "malauzet",
  "password": "supersecret",
  "email": "malauzet@example.com"
}

### Get the user just created (swap 1 for whatever id the register response returned)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### Get a user that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/999

### Register the same username again -> expect 409 (duplicate)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "malauzet",
  "password": "anotherpassword",
  "email": "someoneelse@example.com"
}

### Register with blank username and password -> expect 400 with fieldError map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "password": "",
  "email": "bad@example.com"
}